ments/2494773016","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/99560#issuecomment-2494773016","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/99560","id":2494773016,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6UszcY","user":{"login":"ghost","id":10137,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEwMTM3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/10137?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ghost","html_url":"https://github.com/ghost","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ghost/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ghost/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ghost/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ghost/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ghost/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ghost/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ghost/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ghost/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ghost/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2024-11-22T20:50:08Z","updated_at":"2024-11-22T20:50:08Z","body":"> This might not necessarily be a case for `r_`, the specifics are a bit vague but it is generally used for a returned value, not a modified value, i.e. where the pointer is initialized in the target, take for example `Dictionary::get_key_list`, `Object::get_property_list`, etc.\r\n\r\nOh, I see... Now I also understand why there is discussion label instead of bug...\r\n\r\nBut first of all I am sure I've seen some places where `r_` used in the same way as here. And there is `EditorTranslationParserPlugin::get_recognized_extensions(List<String> *r_extensions)` and some other overrides of the same method in different classes which are already defined with `r_`","author_association":"NONE","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2494773016/reactions